---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const team = [
    {name: "Spencer Barrett", role: "Frontend: Sign Up Page" },
    { name: "Vineet Gupta", role: "Backend (FastAPI)" },
    { name: "Nick Garza", role: "Frontend: Blog Page" },
    { name: "Mikai Miranda", role: "Frontend: About page" },
];
---

<Layout>
    <main class="hero">
        <div class="overlay"></div>
        <div class="content gap-6">
            <h1>Blog <span>BiteSwipe</span></h1>

            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                
            </p>

            <h2>Spencer Barrett</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                “This is a cool product because it helps streamline what I’m looking for.
                A lot of the time I am forced to rely on active recall to think of what food sounds good when I’m hungry.
                Google helps but doesn’t really get me. BiteSwipe helps me find food quickly based on my preferences rather than just what’s nearby.”
            </p>
            <h2>Vineet Gupta</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                I think BiteSwipe is a great idea because it takes the stress out of deciding where to eat.
                I often find myself spending way too much time scrolling through restaurants and trying to figure out what sounds good.
                Having an app that learns my preferences and recommends places based on what I actually enjoy would make the process much easier.
                I also like that BiteSwipe helps users discover new restaurants they might not have considered otherwise.
                Instead of searching through endless options, I can quickly find something that fits my mood, budget, and cravings.
            </p>

            <h2>Nick Garza</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                "I'm the type of person who values quality time with others. BiteSwipe allows me to stay more present when I'm out with friends
                by giving me curated suggestions. The time I would have spent searching through a sea of choices can now be spent in the moment with those around me.
                I believe the best conversations happen over great food and BiteSwipe helps me achieve that."
            </p>

            <h2>Mikai Miranda</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                BiteSwipe gives users a place to take the stress out of deciding where to eat.
                You can swipe through nearby resturaunts the way you would on an app like Tinder.
                You're able to narrow down options by filtering things that matter to you such as the distance, price, or even cuisine.
                Most food apps now give you long, boring lists to scroll through and compare, but with BiteSwipe, you can make a choice quickly and more efficiently.
                This way you can spend less time debating and more time eating. Even if this is for going solo or within a group, BiteSwipe finds the spot. 
            </p>

            <h2>Liam Horgan</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                "BiteSwipe is an app that helps people find places to eat. It gives users information about
                restaurants, including the restaurant’s name, location, food type, rating, price, photos, hours,
                phone number, and website. It can also help users find nearby restaurants. It uses your likes
                and past orders as a reference for future suggestions."
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>